# Exclusions for the `make test-isolation` build context (see the Makefile
# target and this directory's Dockerfile). This is not the repo-root
# .dockerignore: that one excludes test/ entirely, which suits the production
# sqi-server image, while this image needs test/integration/**. The Makefile
# stages a filtered copy of the repo using these patterns rather than relying
# on Docker's per-context .dockerignore discovery, since two Dockerfiles that
# share the repo root as context cannot each have their own automatically
# selected ignore file with the classic (non-BuildKit) builder.
#
# Patterns follow rsync --exclude-from syntax (used by the Makefile target),
# not Docker's .dockerignore glob dialect. Apart from .git/ and
# web/node_modules/, the entries are untracked local dev artifacts that CI and
# a fresh clone never have. Excluding them keeps a multi-gigabyte venv or mypy
# cache out of the staged context on a machine that has run docs tooling or
# the Python clients' tests; COPY . . in the Dockerfile needs only go.mod's
# module tree plus test/integration/.
.git/
web/node_modules/
bin/
.superpowers/
.venv-docs/
.venv/
__pycache__/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
coverage/
# Anchored with a leading /, as rsync --exclude-from reads it. A bare "dist/"
# would also match web/dist/, which must be kept: it holds the git-tracked
# index.html placeholder that //go:embed dist (web/embed.go) needs to compile
# before a web build has run. These two are the local Python build-artifact
# dist directories, as in the repo-root .gitignore's /clients/python/dist/.
/clients/python/dist/
/clients/submitter/dist/
